    <bpmn:process id="W_W4694" name="W4694. Security Incident Response, Crisis Management &amp; Executive Notification" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Significant security incident (attack, kidnap, major theft, data breach convergence, civil-unrest)
Frequency: Rare (preparedness continuous)
Volume: ~ hopefully rare; 1 incident-response/crisis-management framework
Owner: CSO / Crisis Response Lead
Participants: CEO/CFO/Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk (VS-21.2), VP Legal (VS-100.3), Comms (VS-14.3), BCP (VS-26), HR (VS-19), Board (VS-36)
Source: workflow W4694 — Security Incident Response, Crisis Management &amp; Executive Notification</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4694_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4694_Lane1" name="CSO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4694_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4694_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4694_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4694_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4694_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4694_Start3" name="Significant security incident (attack, kidnap, major theft, data breach convergence…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4694_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4694_Task4" name="Maintain the security incident-response &amp; crisis-management framework: severity…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Maintain the security incident-response &amp; crisis-management framework: severity tiers, crisis-response team, activation thresholds, executive-notification cascade, and board-notification protocol (VS-36)
Responsible (R): CSO / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4694_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4694_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4694_Task5" name="On a significant incident: activate the response, establish incident command…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: On a significant incident: activate the response, establish incident command (joint with BCP VS-26, cyber VS-27.3, comms VS-14.3), notify executives/board per threshold, and coordinate resources (law enforcement, insurance VS-26, medevac)
Responsible (R): CSO / Crisis Response Lead / Exec Team
Accountable (A): CEO / Board
Duration: Per incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4694_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4694_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4694_Task6" name="Manage the crisis to resolution; coordinate post-incident review (W4696)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Manage the crisis to resolution; coordinate post-incident review (W4696), insurance/recovery (VS-26), legal (VS-100), and stakeholder/board reporting (VS-36)
Responsible (R): CSO / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk / Legal / Insurance
Accountable (A): CEO / Board
Duration: Per incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4694_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4694_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4694_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4694_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
