    <bpmn:process id="W_W4696" name="W4696. Corporate Security Metrics, Assurance &amp; Post-Incident Review" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Periodic review; post-incident; assurance (VS-21)
Frequency: Monthly/quarterly + post-incident
Volume: 1 corporate-security KPI/KRI set
Owner: CSO
Participants: Internal Audit (VS-21), Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk (VS-21.2), Board Risk Committee (VS-36), Op Excellence (VS-133)
Source: workflow W4696 — Corporate Security Metrics, Assurance &amp; Post-Incident Review</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4696_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4696_Lane1" name="CSO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4696_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4696_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4696_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4696_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4696_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4696_Start3" name="Periodic review; post-incident; assurance (VS-21)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4696_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4696_Task4" name="Maintain corporate-security metrics &amp; KRIs (threat-profile trends, incident…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Maintain corporate-security metrics &amp; KRIs (threat-profile trends, incident frequency/severity, travel-risk exposure, investigation outcomes, EP/GSOC readiness, vendor performance); report to the Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk and board risk committee (VS-36)
Responsible (R): CSO / Analytics
Accountable (A): CSO / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk
Duration: Monthly/quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4696_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4696_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4696_Task5" name="Conduct post-incident reviews (after every significant incident) capturing root…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Conduct post-incident reviews (after every significant incident) capturing root cause, response effectiveness, and corrective actions; feed corrective actions into the program and into VS-21/VS-133
Responsible (R): CSO / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk / Op Excellence
Accountable (A): CSO
Duration: Per incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4696_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4696_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4696_Task6" name="Assure the program via Internal Audit (VS-21) and the physical-security audit…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Assure the program via Internal Audit (VS-21) and the physical-security audit (VS-21.3 W358); continuously improve (VS-133) and refresh the strategy (W4673)
Responsible (R): CSO / Internal Audit
Accountable (A): CSO / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4696_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4696_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4696_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4696_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4696_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-709 (ensure controlled execution — Investigations, Insider Threat, Workplace Violence &amp; Crisis Response (PA-159.3).) | - CTL-709: outcome-oriented KRIs reported to board; post-incident corrective actions tracked; program assured via VS-21
Owner: CSO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
